DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T190000
SUMMARY:The Polyvagal Sangha
DESCRIPTION:Inner Peace Collective\n**The Polyvagal Sangha**\n*A community
  of seekers exploring nervous system regulation through the lens of ancien
 t wisdom and modern science.*\n\nA new tribe is forming. We're inviting 30
  like-minded and like-hearted folks into an ongoing inquiry — learning t
 o cultivate a greater felt sense of calm\, ease\, safety\, and resilience 
 in our bodies\, our relationships\, and the world around us. The goal isn'
 t just personal regulation\, but a ripple effect of co-regulation: a shift
  in how we show up for others and move through our own lives.\n\nThis is t
 he first class in a 3-class series. The whole is greater than the sum of i
 ts parts\, yet a single dive will yield beneficial results towards salutog
 enesis.\n\n**Teachers:** Omri Sitton\, D.C. and Wills Reed\, LCMHCA\n\n**C
 ost:** $10–$15 suggested donation to local nonprofit *Source Of Wellness
 *.\n\\*No one is turned away for lack of funds — all donations are appre
 ciated.\n\n**How to Reserve Your Spot** (please do both — priority goes 
 to folks who complete both steps):\n\n1. **Text Omri at 828-298-0011** wit
 h your name and whether you'd like to pay via Venmo or at the door\n2. **R
 SVP on Meetup** using the button on this page\n\n*A note on the two-step p
 rocess: based on past events\, people who only RSVP on Meetup often don't 
 show up. Texting Omri directly helps us plan for who's actually coming —
  so please do both.*\n\n**A Bit More Detail:**\nPolyvagal Theory (PVT) —
  conceptualized by Stephen Porges — reveals how our body and brain colla
 borate to respond to everyday stress and deeply held trauma. It highlights
  the role of the autonomic nervous system\, especially the vagus nerve\, i
 n shaping our physical and mental health. Paired with mindfulness practice
 s drawn from ancient traditions\, PVT offers us both the science and the f
 elt experience of coming back to our center.\n\nBy building community toge
 ther\, we naturally stimulate the social engagement system — the nervous
  system's highest branch — fostering connection\, safety\, and ease in b
 ody\, mind\, and life. This is the essence of The Polyvagal Sangha.\n\n**P
 articipants will learn:**\n\n* Polyvagal Theory's three defining principle
 s\n* Somatic activities specific to each branch of the autonomic nervous s
 ystem\n* Awareness practices to soften emotional triggers and past traumas
 \n* The body's innate biological responses\, and the role of mindfulness i
 n being present to "what is"\n* How connecting with others committed to pe
 rsonal growth naturally lifts and supports us all\n\nJoin Omri and Wills f
 or a series of illustrated\, experiential presentations that will inspire 
 your spirit\, engage your mind\, and challenge your creativity — as you 
 uncover the enormous potential of applying this work in your daily life.\n
 \n*Feel Well. Heal Well. Live Well.*\n\n**About the teachers:**\n\n**About
  Omri**\nOmri Sitton\, D.C.\, Cert. ZB has 25 years of experience in multi
 ple fields of the healing arts. His passion in helping others has a strong
  emphasis on self-care.\n\nHe naturally weaves the connection between mind
 fulness practice\, cellular consciousness\, and polyvagal theory into his 
 experiential classes.\n\nDr. Omri practices Tonal Chiropractic\, Zero Bala
 ncing\, and Polyvagal Touch in Asheville\, offering what he refers to as C
 hiroSomatics.\nLearn more at [omsourcewellness.com](https://www.omsourcewe
 llness.com/)\n\n**About Wills**\nWills Reed\, LCMHCA\, is an Asheville-bas
 ed psychotherapist with a particular interest in how our earliest relation
 ships\, life experiences\, and nervous systems shape the way we experience
  ourselves and others.\n\nHis work draws from attachment-focused therapy\,
  EMDR\, somatic approaches\, and a longtime personal practice of meditatio
 n and contemplative traditions. He enjoys helping people translate these i
 deas into practical experiences of greater safety\, connection\, and freed
 om in everyday life.
